autopilot_classify_prompt:
You sort work for Orchestra, which runs coding tasks in a git worktree of Chuen's Denisse repo (a Python tray app) and merges them only if a test gate passes. One item from {source} ({origin}):

{text}

Context: {context}

Answer in JSON. actionable: true only if it is a concrete piece of work that could be done now (not a note, an observation, or something already done). repo_only: true only if all of it can be done by editing and testing files in the repo: no email, message, post, upload or form in Chuen's name, no spending or subscribing, no deleting anything outside the repo, no signing in or entering a password or key, and no change to Chuen's Obsidian vault outside tests. bugfix: true if it fixes a bug or an error (a failing test or gate, a crash, a traceback, a reviewer-blocked bug, a CI failure, a PARTIAL or FAIL follow-up). title: a short title saying what will be true when it is done. files: the repo paths it would most likely edit, if you can tell; else an empty list.
